WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.298
The promoter is where transcription begins.

00:00:03.018 --> 00:00:05.572
RNA polymerase makes first contact right here.

00:00:06.419 --> 00:00:08.776
Then proteins open the promoter and unwind

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:09.775
the double helix.

00:00:10.402 --> 00:00:11.864
Now the strands are apart.

00:00:12.155 --> 00:00:13.896
The promoter also sets the direction of

00:00:14.001 --> 00:00:14.442
reading.

00:00:15.069 --> 00:00:16.718
So the RNA builds this way.

00:00:17.345 --> 00:00:18.738
Like a starting gate that points the

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:19.527
race one way.

00:00:20.154 --> 00:00:21.652
Now try the question again.
